{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "ES2022",
    "moduleResolution": "Bundler",
    "lib": [
      "ES2022"
    ],
    "types": [
      "@cloudflare/workers-types",
      "node"
    ],
    "strict": true,
    /*
      AN IMPORT NOTHING USES IS A LIE ABOUT WHAT THIS FILE DEPENDS ON.

      The fidelity gate's `wired` rule proves every EXPORT is referenced and
      says nothing about the other direction, so thirty-eight dead imports
      and locals had accumulated with nothing able to see them. Three of
      them were a `getBeats` round trip per request whose result was thrown
      away; one was a whole UI panel, superseded and still compiled.

      On, so they cannot come back. It costs nothing: an unused parameter is
      exempted by the underscore convention, and `npm run check` typechecks
      first, so this fails the gate rather than a reviewer's attention.
    */
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "verbatimModuleSyntax": false,
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true
  },
  "include": [
    "src/**/*.ts",
    "test/**/*.ts"
  ]
}
